From: artzig <artzig@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] libgui: retire host composer clients after service death

Follow ComposerService and ComposerServiceAIDL death notification, retaining
the dead transport identity on the host. A graphics session cannot reconnect
its original surface/queue objects to a replacement process.

--- a/libs/gui/SurfaceComposerClient.cpp
+++ b/libs/gui/SurfaceComposerClient.cpp
@@ -142,7 +142,14 @@
 void ComposerService::composerServiceDied()
 {
     Mutex::Autolock _l(mLock);
+    // Android reconnects to a restarted system-wide SF. A hosted graphics
+    // session retires on process loss: its old layer/queue identities cannot
+    // attach to a replacement service. Keep the dead proxy so cleanup returns
+    // DEAD_OBJECT even after the broker exits, instead of waiting or returning
+    // a null service to stock callers.
+#ifndef __ANDROID_HOST__
     mComposerService = nullptr;
+#endif
     mDeathObserver = nullptr;
 }
 
@@ -189,7 +196,14 @@
 
 void ComposerServiceAIDL::composerServiceDied() {
     std::scoped_lock lock(mMutex);
+    // Android reconnects to a restarted system-wide SF. A hosted graphics
+    // session retires on process loss: its old layer/queue identities cannot
+    // attach to a replacement service. Keep the dead proxy so cleanup returns
+    // DEAD_OBJECT even after the broker exits, instead of waiting or returning
+    // a null service to stock callers.
+#ifndef __ANDROID_HOST__
     mComposerService = nullptr;
+#endif
     mDeathObserver = nullptr;
 }
 
